{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Look out of [Am]any window, [Em]any morning, [C]any evening, any [G]day.
[D]Maybe the [Am]sun is shining, [Em]birds are winging, [G]No rain is falling from [A]a heavy sky.
[D]What do you [G]want me to do, to [Am]do for you to [Em]see you [D]through?
For [C]this is all a [D]dream we dreamed one [Am]afternoon, long [G]ago.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Walk out of [Am]any doorway, [Em]feel your way, [C]Feel your way like the day [G]before.
[D]Maybe you'll [Am]find direction, [Em]Around some corner [G]where it's been waiting [A]to meet you.
[D]What do you [G]want me to do, [Am]To watch for you while you are [Em][D]sleeping?
Then [Am]please don't be surprised [C]when you [G]find me dreaming [D]too.
{end_of_verse}

