{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Look into [Am]any eyes [Em]you find by you, You can [C]see clear to another [G]day,
[D]Maybe been [Am]seen before, [Em]Through other eyes on [G]other days while going [A]home.
[D]What do you [G]want me to do, to [Am]do for you to [Em]see you [D]through?
It's [C]all a dream we [Em]dreamed one [D]afternoon, long [G]ago.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Walk into [Am]splintered sunlight, [Em]Inch your way [C]through dead dreams to [G]another land.
[D]Maybe you're [Am]tired and broken, [Em]Your tongue is twisted with [G]words half spoken
And [A]thoughts unclear
[D]What do you want [G]me to do, to [Am]do for you to [Em]see you [D]through?
A box of [Am]rain will ease [C]the pain, And love [G]will see you [D]through.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Just a box of rain, [Am]wind and [Em]water,
[C]Believe it if you [A]need it, if you [D]don't, just pass it on
[G]Sun and shower, [Am]wind and [Em]rain,
[C]In and out the [D]window like a [Em]moth before a [A]flame.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
And it's [D]just a box of [Em]rain, I don't [G]know who put it [D]there,
Believe it if you [Bm]need it, or [G]leave it if you [A]dare.
And it's [D]just a box of [Em]rain, or a [G]ribbon for your [D]hair;
Such a [Em]long long time to be gone,
And a [G]short time to be [D]there.[C][G][D][Asus4]
{end_of_verse}
